// Waterbirth Dungeon maze - ambient/filler combat npcs (m28_68/m29_68/m30_68). Migrated from the raw
// 377 cache dump (content/scripts/_unpack/377/all.npc), same pattern as this folder's own
// dagannoth_kings.npc: base appearance/model/anim fields above "op2=Attack" are the untouched raw
// cache values (including a couple of the cache's own quirks, like jb_baby_dagganoth's duplicated
// resizeh/resizev lines - kept verbatim rather than "cleaned up"); everything from op2=Attack onward
// is new, wiring these into skill_combat. Corey (2026-09-03): "all of the npcs in the maze need to be
// aggressive, they all also need their correct attacks, defense, hp, etc".
//
// Real identities confirmed via the OSRS wiki, not assumed from the cache's own tag/name text:
// - dungeon_dagganoth_lighter_deeper (raw vislevel=88) and dungeon_dagganoth_mainroom_deeper (raw
//   vislevel=90) ARE the two real "Dagannoth (Waterbirth Island)" variants - ranged and melee
//   respectively (https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Dagannoth_(Waterbirth_Island)) - it's the raw
//   vislevel matching the wiki's exact combat levels (88/90) that confirmed this, not the cache's
//   generic "lighter"/"mainroom" tag names.
// - giant_rockcrab_deeper (vislevel=137) is the real, already-revealed Giant Rock Crab
//   (https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Giant_Rock_Crab).
// - dagannoth_rock_lobster_2x2 (vislevel=127 - NOT the same tag as the placed "_2x2_loc" variant, see
//   below) is the real, already-revealed Rock Lobster (https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Rock_lobster).
// - dungeon_dagganoth_magic_monster_deeper is actually Wallasalki (real name="Wallasalki" already in
//   the raw cache block) - not a Dagannoth at all despite the tag name. A distinct magic attacker
//   genuinely native to the Waterbirth Island Dungeon per the wiki
//   (https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Wallasalki - "much stronger than their combat level suggests").
// - jb_baby_dagganoth is the real Dagannoth fledgeling
//   (https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Dagannoth_fledgeling) - wiki-confirmed **NOT aggressive**,
//   an intentional exception to "make them all aggressive" to match real behaviour (flagged for Corey
//   to override if he'd rather every single one be hostile regardless).
//
// - dungeon_water_creature_1x1/_1x12/_1x13 are Spinolyp (real name already in the raw cache -
//   https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Spinolyp): HP100/atk10/str10/def10/magic1/ranged100, an
//   aggressive ranged attacker that also drains prayer (real wiki mechanic: "poison damage through
//   its ranged attacks... can drain prayer points with its magic attacks" - implemented here as its
//   ranged hit only, going through the same generic ~npc_rangeattack proc as the other ranged
//   maze npcs; the prayer-drain flavour isn't modelled, no confirmed primitive for it found this
//   pass). Their three raw "Suspicious water" siblings (vislevel=34, no op, non-interactive) are the
//   wiki-documented submerge state Spinolyps cycle into periodically - UPDATE (2026-09-03, round 5,
//   Corey: "for the spinolyps, build the suspicious water stuff"): now fully migrated below with
//   their own weak-melee combat stats, and a real timed emerge/submerge loop is wired in
//   dagannoth_maze_monsters.rs2 (npc_settimer + npc_changetype_keepall, the same self-directed
//   pattern already used for Boulder/Rock). NOTE: neither the visible nor invisible form was found
//   actually placed in any .jm2 map file this project has (searched every region's NPC section for
//   ids 2891-2896, all 660 files, zero placements) - the AI/stats are ready regardless, but there's
//   currently no live spawn point for Corey to test against; flagged rather than guessed at.
//
// Explicitly NOT migrated here, left untouched in all.npc:
// - jb_viking_dude ("Bardur") - a real, named, ordinarily-friendly Fremennik NPC
//   (https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Bardur): "resides deep within the Waterbirth Island Dungeon,
//   where he fights dagannoth fledgelings" (this exact room), tied to The Fremennik
//   Exiles/Trials quests, non-hostile since a 2019 update "to make it easier to talk to him". His raw
//   vislevel=94 matches his old pre-2019 attackable combat level exactly, confirming he's genuine
//   period content, just not a "make it aggressive" filler monster - left alone.
//
// giant_rockcrab_hidden_deeper ("Boulder") and dagannoth_rock_lobster_2x2_loc ("Rock") - UPDATE
// (2026-09-03): Corey reported these aren't aggressive when walked near, and shouldn't wander while
// disguised. Both are now migrated below rather than left in all.npc. Root cause of both symptoms:
// neither had ANY combat/movement fields set, so they fell back to this engine's raw defaults
// (engine/src/cache/config/NpcType.ts: wanderrange defaults to 5, not 0) - explaining the unwanted
// wandering - and with no huntmode at all they could never initiate a reveal on their own, matching
// the same "has combat stats but never attacks" class of bug already found and fixed for the Kings.
// Real OSRS mechanic (https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Giant_Rock_Crab): "disguised as large
// boulders. When approached, they attack" - all.seq has the matching real horror_crab_hide/_reveal
// and dagannoth_rock_lobster_spring_up sequences confirming this is genuine, built content, not a
// guess. Implemented as: wanderrange=0 (stay put while disguised) + a short huntmode/huntrange (1
// tile - "when approached", not a long-range hunt; the wiki gives no exact tile radius, so this
// specific number is a judgment call, not a sourced one) that triggers a self-changetype into the
// already-aggressive revealed form (giant_rockcrab_deeper / dagannoth_rock_lobster_2x2 above) via
// npc_changetype_keepall - see dagannoth_maze_monsters.rs2's ai_queue1 overrides for both. That
// primitive's only confirmed precedent in this codebase is self-directed from an npc's own ai_queue
// hook (content/scripts/macro events/scripts/general/macro_event_triffid.rs2), which this matches.

[dungeon_dagganoth_magic_monster_deeper]
name=Wallasalki
desc=A fearsome magical water creature.
model1=npc_2457
walkanim=wallasalki_walk
readyanim=wallasalki_ready
resizeh=110
resizev=110
op2=Attack
vislevel=98
huntmode=cowardly
huntrange=6
hitpoints=120
attack=1
strength=1
defence=80
magic=100
ranged=1
param=magicattack,100
param=stabdefence,100
param=slashdefence,150
param=crushdefence,175
param=magicdefence,250
param=rangedefence,-10
param=damagetype,^magic_style
param=attackrate,6
param=attackrange,7
param=magicattack_anim,wallasalki_attack
param=defend_anim,wallasalki_defend
param=death_anim,wallasalki_death
param=retreat,0

