// --- "Suspicious water" (Spinolyp's submerge state) - migrated (2026-09-03, round 5) ---
// Corey: "for the spinolyps, build the suspicious water stuff." Real wiki mechanic
// (https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Spinolyp): Spinolyp periodically submerges into this
// unattackable "Suspicious water" state and keeps attacking with a rapid, weak melee hit while
// submerged, before surfacing again. No op1/op2 in the raw cache block (unchanged here, same as
// Boulder/Rock's hidden forms) - kept unattackable by players, but still hunts/retaliates for free
// off the skill_combat wildcard defaults (npc_combat.rs2's [ai_queue1,_]/[ai_opplayer2,_]) same as
// every other plain melee filler npc in this file - op2 only gates PLAYER-initiated attacks, not an
// npc's own outgoing ones (confirmed against npc_combat.rs2's npc_is_attackable vs
// npc_default_attack/npc_check_notcombat this project already read closely), so nothing extra needs
// wiring in dagannoth_maze_monsters.rs2 for the attack itself - just the submerge/emerge timer cycle
// (see that file). Stats below are NOT wiki-sourced (the wiki doesn't break out separate combat
// stats for the submerged state) - a deliberate judgment call for "rapid inaccurate melee attack":
// low accuracy/damage, fast attackrate, crush-style (no ranged/magic while submerged, matching the
// wiki's "while submerged, it can only perform ... a weak melee attack"). wanderrange=0 so it doesn't
// drift out of its water tile while invisible.
[dagannoth_water_creature_1x1_invisible]
name=Suspicious water
desc=If I didn't know better, I'd swear there's something in there...
model1=trollrescue_blankmodel_8
minimap=no
vislevel=34
wanderrange=0
huntmode=cowardly
huntrange=1
hitpoints=100
attack=10
strength=5
defence=10
magic=1
ranged=100
param=stabdefence,10
param=slashdefence,10
param=crushdefence,10
param=magicdefence,20
param=rangedefence,10
param=damagetype,^crush_style
param=attackrate,2
param=attackrange,1
param=defend_anim,dagannoth_water_creature_defend
param=death_anim,dagannoth_water_creature_death
param=retreat,0

